  <h3 id="data-ethics">Data Collection &amp; Ethics</h3>
  <p>
    Videos collected via YouTube Data API v3, CC BY 4.0 only.
    Demographic annotations are <em>perceived</em> attributes from observable characteristics,
    drafted with Gemini 2.5 Flash, fully verified by human experts.
  </p>

  <h3 id="annotation-team">Annotation Team</h3>
  <p>
    Five domain experts (2 PhD, 2 MSc, 1 research scientist), gender-balanced, geographically
    diverse. Hierarchical review with weekly consensus adjudication.
  </p>

  <h3 id="model-configs">Model Configurations</h3>
  <p>
    Open-source: 4&times; A40 (40GB), except MiniCPM-o-2.6 (A100 80GB).
    Gemini: 1 FPS, full audio, API. All: temp=0.7, top-p=0.95, 8192 max tokens.
  </p>

  <h3 id="llm-judge">LLM-as-Judge</h3>
  <p>
    GPT-5-mini scores summaries/rationales 0&ndash;10 for semantic correctness and completeness.
  </p>

  <h3 id="emotional-profiles">Emotional Language Profiles</h3>
  <p>
    LIWC-22 analysis<d-cite key="boyd2022development"></d-cite> of model summaries reveals distinct
    emotional styles: Gemini adopts a clinical tone (high emotional acknowledgment, formal
    delivery); Qwen3-Omni and UniMoE-2.0 are warmer and more supportive; smaller models show
    limited emotional modulation, defaulting to factual reporting.
  </p>
  <figure>
    <iframe src="./diagrams/emotional-language.html" width="100%" height="420" scrolling="no" style="border: none; overflow:hidden;"></iframe>
    <figcaption>Figure A1: Emotional language profiles (LIWC-22 analysis of model summaries).</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h3 id="metrics-primer">Evaluation Metrics</h3>
  <h4>ROUGE-L</h4>
  <d-math block>\text{ROUGE-L}(R, P) = \frac{2 \cdot \text{Prec}_{\text{LCS}} \cdot \text{Rec}_{\text{LCS}}}{\text{Prec}_{\text{LCS}} + \text{Rec}_{\text{LCS}}} \times 100</d-math>
  <h4>Cosine Similarity</h4>
  <d-math block>\text{TextSim}(R, P) = \frac{\mathbf{e}_R \cdot \mathbf{e}_P}{\|\mathbf{e}_R\| \, \|\mathbf{e}_P\|}</d-math>
  <h4>Temporal IoU</h4>
  <d-math block>\text{tIoU}(G, P) = \frac{\max(0, \min(e^{gt}, e^{pred}) - \max(s^{gt}, s^{pred}))}{\max(e^{gt}, e^{pred}) - \min(s^{gt}, s^{pred})}</d-math>
  <h4>Recall@&theta;</h4>
  <d-math block>\text{Recall@}\theta = \frac{1}{N} \sum_{i=1}^{N} \mathbb{1}[\text{tIoU}(G_i, P_i) \geq \theta] \times 100</d-math>
  <h4>MAE</h4>
  <d-math block>\text{MAE}_{\text{avg}} = \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}|s_i^{gt} - s_i^{pred}| + \frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}|e_i^{gt} - e_i^{pred}| \right)</d-math>

